===Etymology 1===
{{root|nn|ine-pro|*ḱerd-}}
From {{der|nn|non|hjarta}}, from {{der|nn|gem-pro|*hertô}}, whence also {{cog|en|heart}}. Ultimately from the {{der|nn|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*ḱerd-}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|nn|hjarte}}
* {{alt|nn|hjerta|hjerte||between the 1938 and 2012 spelling reforms}}

====Noun====
{{nn-noun-irreg|n|hjarta|hjarto|hjarto}}

# [[heart]] (muscle)
#: {{ux|nn|'''Hjarta''' er ein muskel.|The '''heart''' is a muscle.}}
# [[heart]] (seat of emotion)
#: {{usex|nn|'''Hjarta''' mitt vil det annleis.|My '''heart''' wants it different.}}
# {{inflection of|nn|hjarte||p|definite}}

