==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*hertô}}, whence also {{cog|osx|herta}}, {{cog|odt|herta}}, {{cog|ofs|herte}}, {{cog|ang|heorte}}, {{cog|goh|herza}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐍂𐍄𐍉}}. Ultimately from {{der|non|ine-pro|*ḱḗr}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n|hjarta|hjǫrtu}}

# [[heart]]
#* ''[[w:Hávamál|Hávamál]]'' 95 (tr. W. H. Auden and P. B. Taylor):
#*: {{quote|non|Hugr einn þat veit,<br>er býr '''hjarta''' nær,<br>einn er hann sér of sefa;<br>ǫng er sótt verri<br>hveim snotrum manni<br>en sér engu at una.|t=The mind alone knows what is near the '''heart''',<br>Each is his own judge:<br>The worst sickness for a wise man<br>Is to crave what he cannot enjoy.}}

